WEBVTT

00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:02.019
Lolly Tools

00:00:03.014 --> 00:00:07.093
Powerfully reproducible assets & tools.

00:00:07.855 --> 00:00:11.063
Deterministic, fast, open-source platform

00:00:11.096 --> 00:00:13.169
— bring your own brand.

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:16.592
What is Lolly Tools

00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:20.784
A platform that hosts a library of small,

00:00:20.872 --> 00:00:24.018
focused tools that produce deterministic

00:00:24.079 --> 00:00:25.895
creative assets.

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:29.692
Users need no design skill, no vendor

00:00:29.752 --> 00:00:33.036
lock-in and no internet to render, and the

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.906
platform is designed to add premium

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:38.849
production-quality rendering certainty to

00:00:38.921 --> 00:00:40.695
variable data.

00:00:41.447 --> 00:00:45.010
It's also your personal DAM — every logo,

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:47.702
palette, font and upload lives in an

00:00:47.774 --> 00:00:50.543
on-device catalog, hydrated and

00:00:50.645 --> 00:00:53.210
supercharged by your design system and

00:00:53.276 --> 00:00:54.469
tools.

00:00:55.243 --> 00:00:58.319
Tools can be used via a:

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:02.123
Web app - installable offline progressive

00:01:02.191 --> 00:01:03.143
web app

00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:08.394
Mobile and Desktop installable packages.

00:01:08.775 --> 00:01:14.825
and of course, the Command Line — plus a full-screen terminal UI «TUI».

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.818
Why deploy Lolly in your organization?

00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:23.286
Hard-coded constraints of design

00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:24.793
decisions.

00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:33.700
Free, open-source platform — the engine, every shell, the schemas and docs are MPL-2 point 0.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:45.325
Tools and assets are just data: bring your own brand content «SUSE's tool & asset packs are proprietary — see Licensing & structure».

00:01:46.077 --> 00:01:49.444
Unlimited scale, No SaaS fees.

00:01:50.251 --> 00:01:54.069
Low-or-Zero server costs: Lolly uses local

00:01:54.132 --> 00:01:55.893
device compute.

00:01:56.646 --> 00:01:59.888
Builds for Mac, Windows, Linux, iOS,

00:01:59.949 --> 00:02:02.769
Android, web, and the command line.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:09.000
Huge format support — 37 in, 40 out «21 round-trip».

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:37.125
Export: SVG · EPS · CMYK EPS · EMF · DXF · PDF · Print PDF «CMYK» · PPTX · PNG · Animated PNG · JPEG · WebP · Animated WebP · AVIF · TIFF · CMYK TIFF · ICO · PSD · EXR · Radiance HDR · MP4 · WebM · GIF · Animated SVG · MP3 · M4A · WAV · Opus · HTML · MD · TXT · CSV · JSON · ICS · VCF · ZIP.

00:02:37.475 --> 00:02:53.100
Import adds layered PSD · PSB · XCF, HEIC, MOV · Lottie, GLB · glTF, audio & tracker «OGG · FLAC · MIDI · MOD», and live designs from Illustrator · InDesign · Figma · Penpot.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:03:00.600
EXR and Radiance HDR are floating-point HDR masters «via host-codec».

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:12.650
Plus design tokens & palettes — import DTCG and Tokens Studio; export DTCG · ASE · GPL · CSS variables.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:24.850
Print-ready output: CMYK PDF & TIFF, physical units, bleed, crop/registration marks, colour bars, and press «FOGRA/SWOP» profiles.

00:03:25.593 --> 00:03:29.543
Infinite deterministic media creation.

00:03:29.925 --> 00:03:37.650
Renders and exports 100% offline — the shells need no network at render time.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:49.525
«The optional hosted services — MCP agent endpoint, Content Credentials CA — are separate opt-ins; see docs/server-surface-md.»

00:03:50.289 --> 00:03:53.118
Full command-line support.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.981
Save tokens, tell your model to try Lolly

00:03:57.076 --> 00:03:58.170
first!

00:03:59.303 --> 00:04:01.237
What this is not

00:04:02.199 --> 00:04:05.322
A general-purpose design tool

00:04:06.219 --> 00:04:09.352
It does include an open canvas — Layout

00:04:09.413 --> 00:04:12.671
Studio — but even there, colours, type and

00:04:12.733 --> 00:04:15.999
assets conform to the brand globals, so

00:04:16.103 --> 00:04:18.625
free arrangement never becomes off-brand

00:04:18.695 --> 00:04:19.870
output.

00:04:20.657 --> 00:04:23.734
See docs/positioning-md for the full

00:04:23.795 --> 00:04:25.870
landscape comparison.

00:04:27.007 --> 00:04:29.245
Repository layout

00:04:30.242 --> 00:04:33.368
lolly is an umbrella repo: the app core

00:04:33.429 --> 00:04:36.554
lives here, and each shippable unit is a

00:04:36.624 --> 00:04:38.444
git submodule hosted under

00:04:38.506 --> 00:04:41.169
github-com/lolly-tools.

00:04:41.932 --> 00:04:45.109
Every submodule is mounted at its original

00:04:45.188 --> 00:04:48.535
path, so the monorepo builds and runs

00:04:48.599 --> 00:04:50.720
exactly as before.

00:04:51.503 --> 00:04:54.367
Code example omitted.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:05:00.450
Critical separation: engine/ knows nothing about SUSE.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:19.025
Brand-specific content lives in brand packs «brands/suse — private; brands/lolly-start — the blank starter brand», brand-agnostic tools in community/; the shells, services, engine and docs are MPL-2 point 0.

00:05:19.375 --> 00:05:38.775
The repo-root tools/ and catalog/ paths every script and shell consumes are profile views built by scripts/use-profile-ts from profiles-json — switch brands with npm run profile:suse / npm run profile:start.

00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:48.600
Keeping each unit in its own repo lets it ship on its own cadence while the umbrella pins a known-good combination.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.046
Architectural commitments

00:05:52.988 --> 00:05:56.043
These decisions are settled.

00:05:56.802 --> 00:05:59.520
Changing any of them is a major

00:05:59.597 --> 00:06:04.225
undertaking: Declarative tools.

00:06:04.575 --> 00:06:09.475
A tool is a manifest + template + assets.

00:06:09.825 --> 00:06:16.175
Inputs are declared in the manifest, not inferred from template tokens.

00:06:16.525 --> 00:06:26.400
hooks-js is an optional escape hatch for tools that need imperative behavior «chart-js rendering, QR encoding».

00:06:27.143 --> 00:06:30.249
Tools and assets are data, not bundled

00:06:30.337 --> 00:06:31.468
code.

00:06:32.238 --> 00:06:35.267
Clients sync them from a signed manifest

00:06:35.349 --> 00:06:36.743
URL.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:40.640
New tools and assets don't require app

00:06:40.683 --> 00:06:41.943
updates.

00:06:42.711 --> 00:06:45.068
Capability bridge.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:49.212
Tools never touch the filesystem, network,

00:06:49.274 --> 00:06:52.494
or DOM-outside-template directly.

00:06:53.268 --> 00:06:56.218
They call a versioned host.

00:06:56.996 --> 00:06:59.569
* API.

00:07:00.329 --> 00:07:03.027
This is what makes the same tool work in

00:07:03.087 --> 00:07:05.770
browser, Tauri, and CLI.

00:07:06.561 --> 00:07:09.843
Stable asset ID'S forever.

00:07:10.637 --> 00:07:15.094
suse/logo/primary is a contract.

00:07:15.897 --> 00:07:18.844
Never reuse, never rename.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:22.348
Version in the manifest, never in the

00:07:22.419 --> 00:07:23.468
path.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:27.475
URL mode is first-class.

00:07:27.825 --> 00:07:32.825
Every input must be expressible as URL params.

00:07:33.175 --> 00:07:40.200
CLI mode = headless DOM «jsdom» + URL mode + file output.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:43.175
One render path.

00:07:43.525 --> 00:07:46.675
Storage via the bridge.

00:07:47.025 --> 00:07:51.700
Tools call host-state-save«» / host-state-load«».

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:58.225
The bridge picks IndexedDB «web», filesystem «Tauri», or memory «CLI».

00:07:58.575 --> 00:08:01.700
Tools never know which.

00:08:02.456 --> 00:08:04.843
Maturity tags.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:08.516
Every tool declares status: official |

00:08:08.579 --> 00:08:11.119
community | experimental.

00:08:11.894 --> 00:08:14.458
Experimental tools watermark their

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.844
exports.

00:08:16.607 --> 00:08:19.106
This is the structural answer to the

00:08:19.162 --> 00:08:22.119
"brand approved by default" risk.

